      "summary": "The tests check the configured ingress and egress rules but do not verify that the app subnet uses them. A missing or misrouted NSG association can therefore pass the mock-plan assertions while leaving the stated network boundaries unenforced.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/tests/network-boundaries.tftest.hcl",
          "line": 98,
          "message": "The network boundary tests do not verify that the app subnet is associated with the NSG. Add an assertion for the association's subnet_id and network_security_group_id so removing or misrouting it fails the test.",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The ingress and egress assertions inspect the NSG rules, but do not assert that azurerm_subnet_network_security_group_association.app attaches that NSG to the app subnet.",
            "failureScenario": "If the association is removed or points to another subnet, the rule assertions still pass while the app subnet is unprotected by those rules. In particular, unapproved outbound traffic may be allowed, contrary to M-13 and the egress criterion."
          }
        }
      ]
